# Accessibility Standards for Paraguay Tech

## WCAG 2.1 AA Compliance
Ensure all components meet WCAG 2.1 AA standards for accessibility.

## Semantic HTML
- Use proper heading hierarchy (H1 → H2 → H3)
- Use semantic elements (nav, main, section, article, aside, footer)
- Include proper landmarks for screen readers
- Use lists (ul, ol) for related items

## ARIA Attributes
### Required ARIA Labels
- **aria-label**: For interactive elements without visible text
- **aria-describedby**: For additional context
- **aria-expanded**: For collapsible content
- **aria-hidden**: For decorative elements
- **role**: When semantic HTML isn't sufficient

### Example Implementation
```tsx
<Link 
  href="https://discord.gg/ZY5JRnTswv" 
  target="_blank"
  rel="noopener noreferrer"
  aria-label="Únete a nuestra comunidad en Discord"
>
  <Button>Entrar al Discord</Button>
</Link>
```

## Image Accessibility
### Alt Text Requirements
- **Descriptive**: Include context and purpose
- **Concise**: Keep under 125 characters
- **Meaningful**: Describe what's important about the image
- **Empty alt**: Use alt="" for decorative images

### Example
```tsx
<AvatarImage 
  src={moderator.avatar} 
  alt={`Foto de perfil de ${moderator.name}, ${moderator.role} en Paraguay Tech`}
  loading="lazy"
/>
```

## Keyboard Navigation
- Ensure all interactive elements are keyboard accessible
- Use proper tab order
- Include focus indicators
- Implement skip links for main content
- Handle focus management in modals/dropdowns

## Color and Contrast
- Maintain 4.5:1 contrast ratio for normal text
- Maintain 3:1 contrast ratio for large text
- Don't rely solely on color to convey information
- Test with color blindness simulators

## Screen Reader Support
### Hidden Content for SEO
Use screen reader only content for additional context:
```tsx
<div className="sr-only">
  <h2>Comunidad de Desarrolladores en Paraguay</h2>
  <p>Additional context for screen readers and SEO</p>
</div>
```

### Focus Management
- Ensure focus is visible and logical
- Manage focus in dynamic content
- Provide focus indicators
- Handle focus trapping in modals

## Form Accessibility
- Use proper form labels
- Include field descriptions
- Provide error messages
- Use proper input types
- Include required field indicators

## Testing Accessibility
### Manual Testing
- Test with keyboard only navigation
- Use screen reader software
- Check color contrast ratios
- Validate HTML structure

### Automated Testing
- Use axe-core for automated testing
- Include accessibility tests in CI/CD
- Monitor accessibility metrics
- Regular accessibility audits

## Language and Localization
- Use proper lang attributes
- Include language changes in content
- Use proper date/time formats
- Consider RTL languages if needed

## Performance and Accessibility
- Ensure fast loading times
- Provide loading states
- Use progressive enhancement
- Include fallbacks for JavaScript features